  "comments": "<p>The coat of arms of Peru: a shield divided into three parts with a cornucopia on bottom pouring golden coins, a vicuña on top left, and a quinua tree (cinchona officinalis) on top right; civic crown above, a laurel branch on left and a palm branch on right, tied with a ribbon below.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Variants:</strong></p><p>How to understand the difference between wide and narrow dates for 1958:<br>- this one is <strong>wide</strong>:<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/58bc2b7588df8.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/58bc2b7588df8.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br>- and this one is <strong>narrow</strong>:<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/58bc2b9f8b01b.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/58bc2b9f8b01b.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a><br><br>The dates of the 1964 coins<br><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5f8c2e7d6ec74.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5f8c2e7d6ec74.jpg\" alt=\"\"></a></p>",
